**Bug:** This code has a runtime error. `Bun.file(resolvedPath).text()` returns a `Promise<string>`, and you cannot call `.trim()` on a Promise. The `.catch()` handler will never run because the error occurs before it.

The original code wrapped the entire await expression with `.trim()` at the end:
```ts
const fileContent = (
  await Bun.file(resolvedPath)
    .text()
    .catch(...)
).trim()
```

This should be:
```ts
const fileContent = (await Bun.file(resolvedPath).text().catch((error) => {
  const errMsg = `bad file reference: "${match}"`
  if (error.code === "ENOENT") {
    log.warn(`${errMsg}: ${resolvedPath} does not exist, skipping`)
    return ""
  }
  throw new InvalidError({ path: source, message: errMsg }, { cause: error })
})).trim()
```

There is a potential edge case issue here. When `path.parent()` returns `None` for a file path (e.g., a file at the root level or an invalid path), the code falls back to using the original `path` (which is a file) as the directory parameter. This will cause `current_dir()` to fail since it expects a directory. Consider either returning an error when `parent()` is `None` for a file path, or using the current working directory as a fallback instead of the file path itself.
```suggestion
    } else if let Some(parent) = path.parent() {
        parent.to_path_buf()
    } else {
        std::env::current_dir()
            .map_err(|e| format!("Failed to determine current directory: {e}"))?
```

The header capture logic only handles plain object headers and will miss headers if the SDK passes a `Headers` instance or an array of tuples. The condition `typeof init.headers === "object" && !Array.isArray(init.headers)` excludes arrays but will still try to `Object.assign` a `Headers` instance, which may not copy all headers correctly. Consider using `Headers.prototype.forEach` or converting headers to a plain object more robustly to ensure the test captures the anthropic-beta header regardless of the format used by the SDK.
```suggestion
      const rawHeaders = init?.headers
      if (rawHeaders instanceof Headers) {
        rawHeaders.forEach((value, key) => {
          headers[key] = value
        })
      } else if (Array.isArray(rawHeaders)) {
        for (const [key, value] of rawHeaders as Array<[string, string]>) {
          headers[key] = value
        }
      } else if (rawHeaders && typeof rawHeaders === "object") {
        for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(rawHeaders as Record<string, string>)) {
          headers[key] = String(value)
        }
```

